🔹 6. Benefits of Power BI

Easy to learn, especially for Excel users.

Handles large datasets efficiently.

Supports both self-service BI and enterprise BI.

Real-time analytics with live dashboards.

Cross-platform access (desktop, cloud, mobile).

Seamless integration with Microsoft products (Excel, Teams, Azure).

🔹 7. Example Use Cases

📈 Sales Dashboard

Track revenue, profit, monthly growth.

👥 Customer Analytics

Segment customers by region or purchase pattern.

💰 Finance Reporting

Compare budget vs. actuals, monitor expenses.

🏢 HR Analytics

Employee performance, attrition rate, hiring trend.

🔹 8. Conclusion

Power BI is one of the most popular tools for data analysis and visualization.
It enables businesses to make data-driven decisions by converting raw data into interactive insights.

By learning Power BI, you gain skills in:

Data Connectivity

Data Modeling

DAX Calculations

Dashboard Creation

Business Reporting
